<title>UK: Repairs shut Tuapse pipeline, fog closes Ventspils.</title>
<headline>Repairs shut Tuapse pipeline, fog closes Ventspils.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The crude pipeline feeding Russia's 46,000 barrels per day (bpd) refinery at the Black Sea port of Tuapse has been shut for routine maintenance work, a shipping source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The pipeline shut at 0945 local time on Tuesday but loadings of refined oil products continued with two gas oil tankers alongside, the source said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk, Russia's main export terminal on the Black Sea, and Ukraine's port of Odessa were both operating normally.</p>
<p>But the Latvian port of Ventspils on the Baltic was shut by thick fog, the source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
